            <ArticleTitle>Posterior tibial tendon dysfunction and MR imaging in rheumatoid arthritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>38-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a patient with long-standing rheumatoid arthritis and an acute onset of total dysfunction of the posterior tibial tendon. On MRI, a rupture of the tendon was apparent. Intraoperatively, however, massive tenosynovitis with stricture of the tendon was identified as the cause of posterior tibial tendon dysfunction. This case illustrates a pitfall in MRI imaging with potential diagnostic and therapeutic consequences.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
